            <ArticleTitle>[Neoplastic coronary obstruction as an uncommon cause of ischemic cardiopathy. A case description].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>609-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a 64 year-old man suffering from angina caused by neoplastic infiltration of the left anterior descending coronary artery is reported. The coronarographic examination of the vessel disclosed that it had a stenotic segment, which did not move with the cardiac contraction. An aorto-coronary by-pass vein graft relieved the symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
